quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  43,34,"and (likewise, silver) gates for their houses and (silver) couches on which they recline;"
  43,35,"and gold ornamentation (over this silver work). Yet all that would be nothing but temporary enjoyment of the life of this world. And the Hereafter, in the presence of your Lord, is for those who are God-conscious."
  43,36,"And whoever blindly turns away from the remembrance of the Most-Compassionate (Lord), We assign a Satan for him, who remains his close companion."
  43,37,"Indeed, they bar them from the (right) path while they suppose that they are (rightly) guided."
  43,38,"But when he comes to Us, he will say: ‘I wish there had been between me and you the distance of the two easts. What an evil companion (you were)!’"
  43,39,"It will not benefit you on that Day. As you did wrong, so will you share in the punishment."
  43,40,"Can you make the deaf hear then, or guide the blind and the one who is in manifest error?"
  43,41,"Either We shall take you away (from this world) and then take vengeance upon them,"
  43,42,"or We shall show you what We have promised them (as punishment), for indeed We have power over them."
  43,43,"So hold fast to what has been revealed to you. Indeed, you are on the straight path."
  43,44,"Surely, this (Qur’an) is a Reminder for you and your people. (O people!) You will soon be questioned (about it)."
  43,45,Ask (the followers of) those of Our messengers whom We had sent before you. Did We ever appoint any gods to be worshipped besides the Most-Compassionate (Lord)?
  43,46,We indeed sent Musa (Moses) with Our signs to Pharaoh and his notable chiefs. He said: ‘I am a messenger of the Lord of all worlds.’
  43,47,"But when he brought them Our signs, behold, they laughed at them."
